    "verdict": "approved",
    "note": "Final verdict APPROVE after one re-review. The first pass returned REQUEST CHANGES on a single MAJOR: a frontmatter key with whitespace before the mapping colon ('config : 42', legal YAML) bypassed the key-based visual gate because the key tail was not trimmed, so an unrenderable visual contract could draw. The fix trims the key after the colon cut in mermaid_cynefin_impl.cpp; three RED-then-GREEN regression pins cover config/look/theme spacing variants, and the re-review confirmed 21 spacing and near-lookalike variants all fail closed with zero generator/C++ semantic divergence. The same untrimmed-key pattern exists in the already-approved ishikawa/treeview siblings but has no live trigger; per the blast-radius rule it is left for a separate cross-family follow-up, not this change. The reviewer independently reproduced the exact 7/5/0 partition with two separate parsers, ported the validator to a simulator, ran 160 deterministic probes and 300,000 fuzzed inputs with no hang, no fail-open and no verbatim/order invariant break, matched all 30 gtest literals 30/30, and confirmed the single guarded push, the prefix-scoped 1:1 hook and the frozen contracts. The three NITs (indented header accepted, frontmatter-CRLF safe-direction fallback, space-only text transcribed) are fail-closed or faithful, have no corpus sample and match the approved siblings, so they are unchanged."
  },
